/-!
# Solvability by radicals of Galois extensions and polynomials in characteristic zero

Mathlib's `Mathlib.FieldTheory.AbelRuffini` defines the intermediate field `solvableByRad F E` of
elements of `E` solvable by radicals over `F` and proves one implication for irreducible
polynomials: if an irreducible polynomial has a root in `solvableByRad F E`, then its Galois group
is solvable (`isSolvable_gal_of_irreducible`).

This file proves the converse and the resulting equivalences for finite Galois extensions and for
arbitrary polynomials in characteristic zero.

* **Algebra homomorphisms and towers.** Any `F`-algebra homomorphism maps `solvableByRad F E` into
  `solvableByRad F E'`, and `solvableByRad` is transitive in field towers: if the generators of an
  intermediate extension `K / F` lie in `solvableByRad F E`, then `solvableByRad K E` is contained
  in `solvableByRad F E`.
* **Galois extensions with enough roots of unity.** In arbitrary characteristic, if `L / K` is a
  finite Galois extension with solvable Galois group and `K` has enough `[L : K]`-th roots of
  unity, then `solvableByRad K L = ⊤` (`TauCeti.solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isGalois`). The proof
  inducts on `[L : M]` over intermediate fields `M ≤ solvableByRad K L`: a nontrivial finite
  solvable group has a normal subgroup of prime index `p`
  (`Group.IsSolvable.exists_normal_index_prime`), whose fixed field is cyclic of degree `p` over
  `M` and hence generated by a `p`-th root by Kummer theory
  (`exists_root_adjoin_eq_top_of_isCyclic`).
* **Galois extensions in characteristic zero** (`TauCeti.isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad`).
  For a finite Galois extension `E / F` in characteristic zero and an `F`-embedding `ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω`
  into an algebraically closed field `Ω`, `Gal(E/F)` is solvable if and only if every `x : E` has
  `ι x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω`. The ambient algebraically closed field cannot be replaced by `E`
  itself. The reverse implication (`TauCeti.isSolvable_of_forall_mem_solvableByRad`) holds in
  arbitrary characteristic and for any ambient extension `Ω`, via the primitive element theorem and
  `isSolvable_gal_minpoly`.
* **Polynomial criteria** (`TauCeti.isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`). Over a
  field `F` of characteristic zero and an algebraically closed extension `Ω / F`, `q.Gal` is
  solvable if and only if every root of `q` in `Ω` belongs to `solvableByRad F Ω` (including
  `q = 0`, constant polynomials, and reducible or non-squarefree polynomials). When `q` is
  irreducible, solvability of `q.Gal` is also equivalent to the existence of a single root of `q`
  in `solvableByRad F Ω` (`TauCeti.isSolvable_gal_iff_exists_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`).

## Main results

* `AlgHom.map_solvableByRad_le`, `AlgHom.mem_solvableByRad`, `AlgEquiv.map_solvableByRad`,
  `AlgEquiv.mem_solvableByRad`: functoriality of `solvableByRad` under `F`-algebra homomorphisms
  and equivalences.
* `IsPrimitiveRoot.mem_solvableByRad`: primitive `n`-th roots of unity (`n ≠ 0`) lie in
  `solvableByRad`.
* `TauCeti.mem_solvableByRad_of_algebraMap_mem`, `TauCeti.solvableByRad_le_of_le`: monotonicity and
  tower transitivity of `solvableByRad`.
* `TauCeti.solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isGalois`: a finite Galois extension with solvable Galois group
  over a base with enough `[L : K]`-th roots of unity satisfies `solvableByRad K L = ⊤`.
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_of_forall_mem_solvableByRad`: in any characteristic, if an `F`-embedding of
  a finite Galois extension `E / F` lands in `solvableByRad F Ω`, then `Gal(E/F)` is solvable.
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad`: **the radical criterion for finite Galois
  extensions** in characteristic zero (Milne, Theorem 5.34).
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`: **the radical criterion for
  polynomials** in characteristic zero.
* `TauCeti.isSolvable_gal_iff_exists_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad`,
  `TauCeti.forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad_iff_exists`: single-root criteria for irreducible
  polynomials in characteristic zero.
* `TauCeti.forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad_of_natDegree_le_four`: every polynomial of degree at
  most four in characteristic zero has all its roots in `solvableByRad`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Fields and Galois Theory*, v5.10 (2022), Theorem 5.34, p. 77.
-/

public section

open IntermediateField Polynomial

section Functoriality

variable {F E E' : Type*} [Field F] [Field E] [Field E'] [Algebra F E] [Algebra F E']

/-- An `F`-algebra homomorphism maps `solvableByRad F E` into `solvableByRad F E'`. -/
theorem AlgHom.map_solvableByRad_le (φ : E →ₐ[F] E') :
    (solvableByRad F E).map φ ≤ solvableByRad F E' := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  induction hx using solvableByRad.induction with
  | mem a =>
      change φ (algebraMap F E a) ∈ solvableByRad F E'
      rw [φ.commutes]
      exact IntermediateField.algebraMap_mem (solvableByRad F E') a
  | add _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [map_add]
      exact add_mem ih₁ ih₂
  | mul _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ =>
      rw [map_mul]
      exact mul_mem ih₁ ih₂
  | rad n y hn _ ih =>
      exact solvableByRad.rad_mem hn (by rwa [← map_pow])

/-- An `F`-algebra homomorphism preserves membership in `solvableByRad`. -/
theorem AlgHom.mem_solvableByRad (φ : E →ₐ[F] E') {x : E} (hx : x ∈ solvableByRad F E) :
    φ x ∈ solvableByRad F E' :=
  φ.map_solvableByRad_le ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩

/-- An `F`-algebra equivalence identifies `solvableByRad F E` with `solvableByRad F E'`. -/
theorem AlgEquiv.map_solvableByRad (e : E ≃ₐ[F] E') :
    (solvableByRad F E).map e.toAlgHom = solvableByRad F E' := by
  refine le_antisymm e.toAlgHom.map_solvableByRad_le ?_
  rintro x hx
  exact ⟨e.symm x, e.symm.toAlgHom.mem_solvableByRad hx, e.apply_symm_apply x⟩

/-- An `F`-algebra equivalence preserves and reflects membership in `solvableByRad`. -/
@[simp]
theorem AlgEquiv.mem_solvableByRad (e : E ≃ₐ[F] E') {x : E} :
    e x ∈ solvableByRad F E' ↔ x ∈ solvableByRad F E :=
  ⟨fun hx ↦ by
      have h : e.symm (e x) ∈ solvableByRad F E := e.symm.toAlgHom.mem_solvableByRad hx
      rwa [e.symm_apply_apply] at h,
    e.toAlgHom.mem_solvableByRad⟩

/-- For `n ≠ 0`, any primitive `n`-th root of unity in `E` belongs to `solvableByRad F E`. -/
theorem IsPrimitiveRoot.mem_solvableByRad {ζ : E} {n : ℕ} (hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot ζ n)
    (hn : n ≠ 0) : ζ ∈ solvableByRad F E :=
  solvableByRad.rad_mem hn (hζ.pow_eq_one ▸ one_mem _)

end Functoriality

namespace TauCeti

section Tower

/-- **Monotonicity of `solvableByRad` in the base field.** Given field extensions `E / F` and
`E / K`, if `algebraMap K E` maps every element of `K` into `solvableByRad F E`, then every element
of `solvableByRad K E` also lies in `solvableByRad F E`. -/
theorem mem_solvableByRad_of_algebraMap_mem {F K E : Type*} [Field F] [Field K] [Field E]
    [Algebra K E] [Algebra F E] (hK : ∀ k : K, algebraMap K E k ∈ solvableByRad F E) {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ solvableByRad K E) : x ∈ solvableByRad F E := by
  induction hx using solvableByRad.induction with
  | mem k => exact hK k
  | add _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ => exact add_mem ih₁ ih₂
  | mul _ _ _ _ ih₁ ih₂ => exact mul_mem ih₁ ih₂
  | rad n _ hn _ ih => exact solvableByRad.rad_mem hn ih

/-- **Transitivity of `solvableByRad` in field towers.** If an intermediate field `K` of `E / F` is
contained in `solvableByRad F E`, then every element of `solvableByRad K E` lies in
`solvableByRad F E`. -/
theorem solvableByRad_le_of_le {F E : Type*} [Field F] [Field E] [Algebra F E]
    {K : IntermediateField F E} (hK : K ≤ solvableByRad F E) :
    (solvableByRad K E).restrictScalars F ≤ solvableByRad F E :=
  fun _ hx ↦ mem_solvableByRad_of_algebraMap_mem (fun k ↦ hK k.2) hx

end Tower

section Galois

/-- **Radical generation with enough roots of unity.** In any characteristic, if `L / K` is a
finite Galois extension with solvable Galois group and `K` has enough `[L : K]`-th roots of unity,
then every element of `L` is solvable by radicals over `K`. -/
theorem solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isGalois (K L : Type*) [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra K L]
    [FiniteDimensional K L] [IsGalois K L] [Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[K] L)]
    [HasEnoughRootsOfUnity K (Module.finrank K L)] :
    solvableByRad K L = ⊤ := by
  have hN : NeZero (Module.finrank K L) := ⟨Module.finrank_pos.ne'⟩
  -- Induct on `[L : M]` over intermediate fields `M ≤ solvableByRad K L`.
  suffices ∀ d : ℕ, ∀ M : IntermediateField K L,
      Module.finrank M L = d → M ≤ solvableByRad K L → solvableByRad K L = ⊤ by
    exact this (Module.finrank (⊥ : IntermediateField K L) L) ⊥ rfl bot_le
  intro d
  induction d using Nat.strongRecOn with
  | ind d ih =>
    intro M hd hM
    have hML_pos : 0 < Module.finrank M L := Module.finrank_pos
    by_cases hd1 : d ≤ 1
    · have h1 : Module.finrank M L = 1 := by omega
      exact top_unique (IntermediateField.finrank_eq_one_iff_eq_top.mp h1 ▸ hM)
    · have : IsGalois M L := IsGalois.tower_top_of_isGalois K M L
      have : Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[M] L) :=
        Group.isSolvable_of_isSolvable_injective (AlgEquiv.restrictScalarsHom_injective K)
      have hcard : Nat.card (L ≃ₐ[M] L) = d := by rw [IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank, hd]
      have : Nontrivial (L ≃ₐ[M] L) := Finite.one_lt_card_iff_nontrivial.mp (by omega)
      -- Descend along a normal subgroup `H` of `Gal(L/M)` of prime index `p`.
      obtain ⟨H, _, hp⟩ := Group.IsSolvable.exists_normal_index_prime (L ≃ₐ[M] L)
      let M' : IntermediateField M L := IntermediateField.fixedField H
      have : IsGalois M M' := IsGalois.of_fixedField_normal_subgroup H
      have hquot_card : Nat.card ((L ≃ₐ[M] L) ⧸ H) = H.index := H.index_eq_card.symm
      have hM'_card : Nat.card (M' ≃ₐ[M] M') = H.index :=
        (Nat.card_congr (IsGalois.normalAutEquivQuotient H).symm.toEquiv).trans hquot_card
      have hfin_M' : Module.finrank M M' = H.index := by
        rw [← IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank, hM'_card]
      have : Fact H.index.Prime := ⟨hp⟩
      have : IsCyclic ((L ≃ₐ[M] L) ⧸ H) := isCyclic_of_prime_card hquot_card
      have : IsCyclic (M' ≃ₐ[M] M') :=
        isCyclic_of_surjective _ (IsGalois.normalAutEquivQuotient H).surjective
      -- `p = [M' : M]` divides `[L : K]`, so `M` contains a primitive `p`-th root of unity.
      have hdvd : Module.finrank M M' ∣ Module.finrank K L := by
        refine dvd_trans ⟨Module.finrank M' L, (Module.finrank_mul_finrank M M' L).symm⟩ ?_
        exact ⟨Module.finrank K M, by rw [mul_comm, Module.finrank_mul_finrank K M L]⟩
      have : HasEnoughRootsOfUnity M (Module.finrank K L) := inferInstance
      have : HasEnoughRootsOfUnity M (Module.finrank M M') :=
        HasEnoughRootsOfUnity.of_dvd M hdvd
      have : NeZero (Module.finrank M M') := ⟨by rw [hfin_M']; exact hp.ne_zero⟩
      obtain ⟨α, ⟨m, hm⟩, hα_top⟩ := exists_root_adjoin_eq_top_of_isCyclic M M'
        (HasEnoughRootsOfUnity.primitiveRoots_nonempty M (Module.finrank M M'))
      -- `(α : L) ^ p ∈ M ≤ solvableByRad K L`, so `M'` lies in `solvableByRad K L`.
      have hα_rad : (α : L) ∈ solvableByRad K L := by
        refine solvableByRad.rad_mem (n := Module.finrank M M') (NeZero.ne _) ?_
        have hpow : (α : L) ^ Module.finrank M M' = (m : L) := by
          have h := congrArg M'.val hm.symm
          rw [map_pow, M'.val.commutes] at h
          exact h
        exact hpow ▸ hM m.2
      let M'_K : IntermediateField K L := M'.restrictScalars K
      have hM'_le : M'_K ≤ solvableByRad K L := by
        intro x hx
        have hx_top : (⟨x, hx⟩ : M') ∈ (⊤ : IntermediateField M M') := trivial
        rw [← hα_top] at hx_top
        have hx_map : x ∈ (M⟮α⟯).map M'.val := ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hx_top, rfl⟩
        rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_map, Set.image_singleton] at hx_map
        let S : IntermediateField M L :=
          { (solvableByRad K L).toSubfield with
            algebraMap_mem' r := hM r.2 }
        exact (IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff (F := M) (E := L) (K := S)).mpr hα_rad hx_map
      have hM'L_lt : Module.finrank M'_K L < d := by
        have hmul : Module.finrank M M' * Module.finrank M' L = d := by
          rw [Module.finrank_mul_finrank M M' L, hd]
        have hp_gt : 1 < Module.finrank M M' := by rw [hfin_M']; exact hp.one_lt
        have : 0 < Module.finrank M' L := Module.finrank_pos
        change Module.finrank M' L < d
        nlinarith
      exact ih (Module.finrank M'_K L) hM'L_lt M'_K rfl hM'_le

/-- **From radical embeddings to solvable Galois groups.** In any characteristic, if `E / F` is a
finite Galois extension and `ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω` maps every element of `E` into `solvableByRad F Ω` for
some extension `Ω / F`, then `Gal(E/F)` is solvable. -/
theorem isSolvable_of_forall_mem_solvableByRad {F E Ω : Type*} [Field F] [Field E] [Field Ω]
    [Algebra F E] [Algebra F Ω] [FiniteDimensional F E] [IsGalois F E] (ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω)
    (h : ∀ x : E, ι x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω) :
    Group.IsSolvable (E ≃ₐ[F] E) := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := Field.exists_primitive_element F E
  have : (minpoly F α).IsSplittingField F E :=
    isSplittingField_minpoly_of_adjoin_simple_eq_top α hα
  have hmin : minpoly F (ι α) = minpoly F α := minpoly.algHom_eq ι ι.injective α
  have hsol : Group.IsSolvable (minpoly F α).Gal := hmin ▸ isSolvable_gal_minpoly (h α)
  exact (MulEquiv.isSolvable_congr (IsSplittingField.algEquiv E (minpoly F α)).autCongr).mpr hsol

/-- **The radical criterion for finite Galois extensions** (Milne, *Fields and Galois Theory*,
Theorem 5.34). In characteristic zero, a finite Galois extension `E / F` has solvable Galois group
if and only if under an `F`-embedding `ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω` into an algebraically closed extension `Ω`
(for example `AlgebraicClosure F` or `ℂ`), every element of `E` maps into `solvableByRad F Ω`. -/
theorem isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad {F E Ω : Type*} [Field F] [CharZero F]
    [Field E] [Algebra F E] [FiniteDimensional F E] [IsGalois F E] [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω]
    [IsAlgClosed Ω] (ι : E →ₐ[F] Ω) :
    Group.IsSolvable (E ≃ₐ[F] E) ↔ ∀ x : E, ι x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω := by
  refine ⟨fun hsol x ↦ ?_, isSolvable_of_forall_mem_solvableByRad ι⟩
  -- Embed `E` as `K = ι.fieldRange` inside `Ω`, adjoin a primitive `[E : F]`-th root of unity `ζ`,
  -- and apply `solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isGalois` to the Galois compositum `K ⊔ F⟮ζ⟯ / F⟮ζ⟯`.
  let K : IntermediateField F Ω := ι.fieldRange
  let eK : E ≃ₐ[F] K := AlgEquiv.ofInjectiveField ι
  have : FiniteDimensional F K := eK.toLinearEquiv.finiteDimensional
  have : IsGalois F K := IsGalois.of_algEquiv eK
  have hK_sol : Group.IsSolvable (K ≃ₐ[F] K) :=
    (MulEquiv.isSolvable_congr eK.autCongr).mp hsol
  let N : ℕ := Nat.card (K ≃ₐ[F] K)
  have hN_pos : 0 < N := Nat.card_pos
  have : NeZero N := ⟨hN_pos.ne'⟩
  have : CharZero Ω := charZero_of_injective_algebraMap (algebraMap F Ω).injective
  obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ := HasEnoughRootsOfUnity.exists_isPrimitiveRoot Ω N
  let Fζ : IntermediateField F Ω := F⟮ζ⟯
  let L : IntermediateField F Ω := K ⊔ Fζ
  have : FiniteDimensional F Fζ :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin.finiteDimensional (hζ.isIntegral hN_pos).tower_top
  have : FiniteDimensional F L := inferInstanceAs (FiniteDimensional F ↥(K ⊔ Fζ))
  -- Inside `L = K ⊔ Fζ`, restrict `K` and `Fζ` so `K_in_L ⊔ Fζ_in_L = ⊤`.
  let K_in_L : IntermediateField F L := K.restrict le_sup_left
  let Fζ_in_L : IntermediateField F L := Fζ.restrict le_sup_right
  have hsup_top : K_in_L ⊔ Fζ_in_L = ⊤ := by
    rw [← IntermediateField.lift_inj, IntermediateField.lift_top, IntermediateField.lift_sup,
      IntermediateField.lift_restrict le_sup_left, IntermediateField.lift_restrict le_sup_right]
  let eKL : K_in_L ≃ₐ[F] K :=
    (IntermediateField.liftAlgEquiv K_in_L).trans
      (IntermediateField.equivOfEq (IntermediateField.lift_restrict le_sup_left))
  have : FiniteDimensional F K_in_L := eKL.symm.toLinearEquiv.finiteDimensional
  have : IsGalois F K_in_L := IsGalois.of_algEquiv eKL.symm
  have : Group.IsSolvable (K_in_L ≃ₐ[F] K_in_L) :=
    (MulEquiv.isSolvable_congr eKL.autCongr).mpr hK_sol
  have : IsGalois Fζ_in_L L := IsGalois.sup_right K_in_L Fζ_in_L hsup_top
  have hinj := IntermediateField.restrictRestrictAlgEquivMapHom_injective K_in_L Fζ_in_L hsup_top
  have : Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[Fζ_in_L] L) := Group.isSolvable_of_isSolvable_injective hinj
  -- `[L : Fζ_in_L]` divides `N = |Gal(K/F)|`, and `Fζ_in_L` contains the primitive `N`-th root `ζ`.
  have hdvd : Module.finrank Fζ_in_L L ∣ N := by
    rw [← IsGalois.card_aut_eq_finrank]
    have hdvd' : Nat.card (L ≃ₐ[Fζ_in_L] L) ∣ Nat.card (K_in_L ≃ₐ[F] K_in_L) :=
      Subgroup.card_dvd_of_injective _ hinj
    rwa [Nat.card_congr eKL.autCongr.toEquiv] at hdvd'
  have hζ_L : ζ ∈ L := (le_sup_right : Fζ ≤ L) (IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_self F ζ)
  have hζ_mem : (⟨ζ, hζ_L⟩ : L) ∈ Fζ_in_L :=
    (IntermediateField.mem_restrict le_sup_right _).mpr
      (IntermediateField.mem_adjoin_simple_self F ζ)
  have hζL_prim : IsPrimitiveRoot (⟨ζ, hζ_L⟩ : L) N := by
    rwa [← IsPrimitiveRoot.map_iff_of_injective L.val.injective]
  have hζ_Fζ : IsPrimitiveRoot (⟨⟨ζ, hζ_L⟩, hζ_mem⟩ : Fζ_in_L) N := by
    rwa [← IsPrimitiveRoot.map_iff_of_injective Fζ_in_L.val.injective]
  have : HasEnoughRootsOfUnity Fζ_in_L N :=
    { prim := ⟨_, hζ_Fζ⟩
      cyc := rootsOfUnity.isCyclic Fζ_in_L N }
  have : HasEnoughRootsOfUnity Fζ_in_L (Module.finrank Fζ_in_L L) :=
    HasEnoughRootsOfUnity.of_dvd Fζ_in_L hdvd
  have htop : solvableByRad Fζ_in_L L = ⊤ := solvableByRad_eq_top_of_isGalois Fζ_in_L L
  -- `Fζ_in_L ≤ solvableByRad F L`, so `solvableByRad_le_of_le` and `L.val` land in `solvableByRad`.
  have hFζ_rad : Fζ_in_L ≤ solvableByRad F L := by
    intro y hy
    have hy' : (y : Ω) ∈ (F⟮(⟨ζ, hζ_L⟩ : L)⟯).map L.val := by
      rw [IntermediateField.adjoin_map, Set.image_singleton]
      exact (IntermediateField.mem_restrict le_sup_right y).mp hy
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hzy⟩ := hy'
    have hzy' : z = y := L.val.injective hzy
    exact IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_le_iff.mpr
      (hζL_prim.mem_solvableByRad hN_pos.ne') (hzy' ▸ hz)
  have hx_L : ι x ∈ L := (le_sup_left : K ≤ L) ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have hxL : (⟨ι x, hx_L⟩ : L) ∈ solvableByRad Fζ_in_L L := by
    rw [htop]
    trivial
  exact L.val.mem_solvableByRad (solvableByRad_le_of_le hFζ_rad hxL)

end Galois

section Polynomial

/-- **The radical criterion for polynomials.** In characteristic zero, for any algebraically closed
extension `Ω / F` (such as `AlgebraicClosure F` or `ℂ`) and any polynomial `q : F[X]`, the Galois
group `q.Gal` is solvable if and only if every root of `q` in `Ω` lies in `solvableByRad F Ω`.

This applies unconditionally to `q = 0`, constant polynomials, and polynomials with repeated or
reducible factors. -/
theorem isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad {F : Type*} (Ω : Type*) [Field F]
    [CharZero F] [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] (q : F[X]) :
    Group.IsSolvable q.Gal ↔ ∀ x ∈ q.rootSet Ω, x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω := by
  let L : IntermediateField F Ω := IntermediateField.adjoin F (q.rootSet Ω)
  have : q.IsSplittingField F L :=
    IntermediateField.adjoin_rootSet_isSplittingField (IsAlgClosed.splits _)
  have : FiniteDimensional F L := IsSplittingField.finiteDimensional L q
  have : Normal F L := Normal.of_isSplittingField q
  have : IsGalois F L := ⟨⟩
  have hgal : Group.IsSolvable q.Gal ↔ Group.IsSolvable (L ≃ₐ[F] L) :=
    (MulEquiv.isSolvable_congr (IsSplittingField.algEquiv L q).autCongr).symm
  rw [hgal, isSolvable_iff_forall_mem_solvableByRad L.val]
  -- Unfold subtype quantification over `L = F(q.rootSet Ω)` via `adjoin_le_iff`.
  exact ⟨fun h x hx ↦ h ⟨x, IntermediateField.subset_adjoin F _ hx⟩,
    fun h y ↦ IntermediateField.adjoin_le_iff.mpr h y.2⟩

/-- **Single-root radical criterion for irreducible polynomials.** In characteristic zero, an
irreducible polynomial `q : F[X]` has solvable Galois group if and only if at least one root of `q`
in an algebraically closed extension `Ω / F` lies in `solvableByRad F Ω`. -/
theorem isSolvable_gal_iff_exists_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad {F : Type*} (Ω : Type*) [Field F]
    [CharZero F] [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] {q : F[X]} (hq : Irreducible q) :
    Group.IsSolvable q.Gal ↔ ∃ x ∈ q.rootSet Ω, x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω := by
  refine ⟨fun hsol ↦ ?_, fun ⟨x, hx, hrad⟩ ↦
    isSolvable_gal_of_irreducible hrad hq (aeval_eq_zero_of_mem_rootSet hx)⟩
  have hdeg : (q.map (algebraMap F Ω)).degree ≠ 0 := by
    rw [degree_map_eq_of_injective (algebraMap F Ω).injective]
    exact hq.degree_pos.ne'
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (IsAlgClosed.splits (q.map (algebraMap F Ω))).exists_eval_eq_zero hdeg
  have hx_root : x ∈ q.rootSet Ω := by
    rw [mem_rootSet_of_ne hq.ne_zero, aeval_def, ← eval_map]
    exact hx
  exact ⟨x, hx_root,
    (isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad Ω q).mp hsol x hx_root⟩

/-- For an irreducible polynomial in characteristic zero, one root in an algebraically closed
extension `Ω / F` is solvable by radicals if and only if all of its roots in `Ω` are. -/
theorem forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad_iff_exists {F Ω : Type*} [Field F] [CharZero F]
    [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] {q : F[X]} (hq : Irreducible q) :
    (∀ x ∈ q.rootSet Ω, x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω) ↔ ∃ x ∈ q.rootSet Ω, x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω := by
  rw [← isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad Ω q,
    isSolvable_gal_iff_exists_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad Ω hq]

/-- In characteristic zero, every polynomial of degree at most four has all of its roots in an
algebraically closed extension solvable by radicals. -/
theorem forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad_of_natDegree_le_four {F Ω : Type*} [Field F] [CharZero F]
    [Field Ω] [Algebra F Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] {q : F[X]} (hq : q.natDegree ≤ 4) :
    ∀ x ∈ q.rootSet Ω, x ∈ solvableByRad F Ω :=
  (isSolvable_gal_iff_forall_rootSet_mem_solvableByRad Ω q).mp
    (Polynomial.isSolvable_gal_of_natDegree_le_four hq)

end Polynomial

end TauCeti
